# Think, then recheck

Name the blast radius before editing: the page, its API route, the hub that owns it, the offline snapshot name, and every caller of the symbol you will change.

Match an existing pattern in this repo. The smallest change that fits the surrounding code is the one to make.

After the edit, and again after the last fix:

1. Re-read the full diff. Confirm it does not revert a comment, a guard, or another agent's hunk.
2. Find every importer of the symbol you changed. A shared helper is not done when one caller still compiles in your head.
3. Use the changed flow on https://vantagefrc.vercel.app, then open the neighboring route that shares the shell, hub, or data.

A single look is not a check. If the diff, a caller, and the live page disagree, fix that before reporting done.

On this laptop, do not start a local database, dev server, test runner, or build unless the user explicitly authorizes that workload. Read the existing tests that name the symbol. Do not rewrite them to match a new behavior unless the task changed that behavior.
